@node Intro "Introduction"

  @{b}Introduction@{ub}

  Formbröd is a video editor for AmigaOS 4. Add video files, sound files
  and pictures, cut them, put them in order, add fades and crossfades,
  and export the result as a movie file.

  Reading and writing video is done by the ffmpeg libraries, which are
  built into the program. Nothing else needs installing.

  Every action in the window can also be done from @{" ARexx " link ARexx}.

  This is an early version, and has been developed using AI (Claude).
  The program has been tested on AmigaOS 4 on AmigaOne X1000 and
  micro-AmigaOne. Most features have been tested and verified on Linux.

@endnode

@node Requirements "Requirements"

  @{b}Requirements@{ub}

  - AmigaOS 4.1
  - AHI, for sound when previewing
  - Enough memory for the videos you edit. Previews use small copies
    of the files, so editing needs far less than exporting.

  The toolbar uses the AISS icons in TBImages:.

@endnode

@node Install "Installation"

  @{b}Installation@{ub}

  Unpack the archive anywhere, open the Formbrod drawer and double-click
  @{b}Install-Formbrod@{ub}. Choose where to put it; a drawer called
  Formbrod is made there.

  To update, install over the old drawer. Your settings and the cache
  are kept.

  You can also just drag the Formbrod drawer wherever you like.

  The Catalogs drawer holds the translations. Keep it next to the
  program, or copy its contents to LOCALE:Catalogs/.

@endnode

@node QuickStart "Quick start"

  @{b}Quick start@{ub}

  1. Click @{b}Add file@{ub} and choose a video. It appears on a track of
     its own, and its film strip is drawn above the tracks.
  2. Choose @{b}Track > Append file...@{ub} to add a second video after
     the first on the same track. Or drop it on the track from Workbench.
  3. Move the playhead to where the first video should end and press
     @{b}O@{ub} (Set out).
  4. Press @{b}Space@{ub} to play the result in the preview window.
  5. Click @{b}Export@{ub} and give a file name. Progress is shown at the
     bottom of the window.

@endnode

@node Window "The window"

  @{b}The window@{ub}

  @{b}Toolbar@{ub}
  Add file, Split, Remove, Fade, Crossfade, Play and Export. Hold the
  mouse over a button to see what it does. Set in and Set out are in the
  Edit menu, and on the I and O keys.

  @{b}Ruler and film strip@{ub}
  The film strip shows the finished edit with a picture a second. Click
  or drag in it, or in the ruler, to move the playhead. The zoom control
  sets how much of the edit fits in the window.

  @{b}Overview@{ub}
  The whole edit at once. Its two flags mark a range, used by
  @{" Export range " link Paint}.

  @{b}Tracks@{ub}
  Under the film strip is one row per track: Video 1, Audio 1 and so
  on. A video track's sound is on a lane under it, with its waveform.
  Higher video tracks are drawn on top of lower ones; all sound is
  mixed.

  @{b}Clip fields@{ub}
  Starts, From file and Length of the selected clip. Type 1:05.5 or
  plain seconds like 12.5 and press Return.

@endnode

@node Editing "Editing"

  @{b}Editing@{ub}

  @{b}Adding@{ub}
  Add file puts a video, a sound file or a picture on a new track. A
  picture starts out 5 seconds long and can be made any length. Files
  dropped on a track are added after its last clip; files dropped below
  the tracks get a track each.

  @{b}Selecting@{ub}
  Click a clip to select it. Click a track's name to select the track
  for the Track menu (Append file, Mute audio, Hide video, Remove track).

  @{b}Trimming@{ub}
  Drag either end of a clip. Or put the playhead in it and use
  @{b}Set in@{ub} (I) to cut away its start, or @{b}Set out@{ub} (O) to
  cut away its end. With the playhead after a clip's end, Set out makes
  it longer, as far as its file goes. The clips after it move along, so
  no gap is left.

  @{b}Splitting@{ub}
  Split cuts the selected clip at the playhead. With nothing selected,
  every track is cut there.

  @{b}Moving@{ub}
  Drag the middle of a clip. An outline shows where it lands: where you
  drop it if there's room, otherwise between the clips at the orange
  line. Ends snap to other clips, the start and the playhead. Drop it
  below the tracks to give it a track of its own. The right mouse button
  cancels.

  @{b}Fitting@{ub}
  Clips of different size and frame rate can be mixed. Each is fitted to
  the project's frame: inside with bars, filling it and cropping, or
  stretched. Set the default under Settings > Fit clips to frame, or per
  clip in the clip window.

  @{b}Clip window@{ub}
  Double-click a clip (or Edit > Clip settings...) for all its settings:
  timing, fades, crossfade, fit, volume and effects. It follows the
  selection.

@endnode

@node Effects "Effects"

  @{b}Effects@{ub}

  @{b}Fades@{ub}
  The Fade button fades the selected clip in over one second. Set fade
  in and fade out lengths in the clip window.

  @{b}Crossfades@{ub}
  The Crossfade button fades over to the selected clip from the one
  before it on its track. The clips overlap, drawn with an X. Choose the
  kind (fade, wipes, slides, circle...) under Edit > Crossfade kind.
  Click Crossfade again for a plain cut.

  @{b}Modules@{ub}
  The Effects menu lists the effect modules. Each effect's settings get
  fields in the clip window.

  @{b}Volume@{ub}
  Per clip in the clip window, 100% being as recorded.

@endnode

@node Preview "Previewing"

  @{b}Previewing@{ub}

  Space plays from the playhead in the preview window, with sound, and
  stops again. When not playing, the window shows the frame at the
  playhead. Project > Show preview window opens it.

  To keep editing smooth, each video gets a small copy (a proxy) made in
  the background the first time it's added. Previews are rendered from
  these. Settings > Make preview copies and Preview copy size control
  this. With Render previews in the background on, the edit is rendered
  ahead so playing starts at once.

@endnode

@node Export "Exporting"

  @{b}Exporting@{ub}

  Project > Project settings... sets the frame (size, frame rate, how
  clips fit) and what export writes: video codec and quality, sound and
  bit rate, and the kind of file.

  Export renders the whole edit at full quality from the original files.
  Cancel render stops it; the file it was writing is not finished.

@endnode

@node Paint "Paint programs"

  @{b}Paint programs@{ub}

  @{b}Save frame...@{ub} (Project menu) saves the frame at the playhead as
  an IFF ILBM or PNG. Draw on it as a stencil, and the picture lines up
  with the film.

  For effects drawn frame by frame, mark a range with the overview's
  flags (or Edit > Range starts here / Range ends here) and choose
  Project > @{b}Export range...@{ub}. It is written small, as an IFF ANIM, or as
  a movie if the name ends in .mp4, .gif and so on.

@endnode

@node Projects "Projects"

  @{b}Projects@{ub}

  New, Open project... and Save project in the Project menu. A project
  is a plain text file listing the files used and how they're edited. It
  can be read and edited in a text editor. The video files themselves
  are not copied, so keep them where they are.

@endnode

@node Settings "Settings"

  @{b}Settings@{ub}

  The Settings menu holds the program's own settings.

  - Fit clips to frame: the default for new clips
  - Show frame pictures: thumbnails in the film strip
  - Make preview copies / Preview copy size
  - Render previews in the background
  - Write log file: to T:Formbrod.log. Include it when reporting a
    problem.

  @{b}Cache@{ub}
  Preview copies, thumbnails and waveforms are kept in the Cache drawer
  next to the program (PROGDIR:Cache). It can be deleted at any time;
  it's made again when needed.

@endnode

@node ARexx "ARexx"

  @{b}ARexx@{ub}

  The port is called @{b}FORMBROD@{ub}. Times are in milliseconds, clips
  and tracks are numbered from 0.

  /* Join two files, fade in the first, and export */
  ADDRESS FORMBROD
  'OPEN "Work:Video/intro.mp4"'
  track = RESULT
  'APPEND' track '"Work:Video/main.mp4"'
  'EFFECT 0 fade'
  'SETPARAM 0' RESULT 'in 2.0'
  'EXPORT "Work:Video/final.mp4"'
  DO UNTIL LEFT(RESULT, 7) ~= 'RUNNING'
      'RENDERSTATUS'
      ADDRESS COMMAND 'Wait 1'
  END

  @{b}Files and projects@{ub}
  OPEN FILE/A                    add a file on a new track; gives the track
  APPEND TRACK/N/A,FILE/A        add a file after a track's last clip
  NEWPROJECT, OPENPROJECT FILE/A, SAVEPROJECT FILE
  QUIT

  @{b}Editing@{ub}
  TRACKS, CLIPS                  how many there are
  SPLIT AT/N/A,TRACK/N           all tracks if TRACK is left out
  TRIM CLIP/N/A,IN/N,OUT/N       times in the clip's file
  MOVE CLIP/N/A,AT/N/A,TRACK/N   like dragging it
  REMOVE CLIP/N/A
  FIT CLIP/N/A,MODE/A
  VOLUME CLIP/N/A,PERCENT/N/A    100 = as recorded, up to 400
  PLAYHEAD AT/N                  moves it if AT is given; gives its time

  @{b}Effects@{ub}
  MODULES                        the effect modules' names
  EFFECT CLIP/N/A,MODULE/A       gives the effect's number
  SETPARAM CLIP/N/A,EFFECT/N/A,NAME/A,VALUE/A
  REMOVEEFFECT CLIP/N/A,EFFECT/N/A
  FADES CLIP/N/A,IN/N,OUT/N
  CROSSFADE CLIP/N/A,LENGTH/N/A,KIND/K   KIND: fade, wipeleft, ...

  @{b}Preview@{ub}
  PLAY AT/N,STOP/S
  PREVIEW AT/N,STOP/S
  RENDERAHEAD ON/S,OFF/S
  CACHE ON/S,OFF/S,WIDTH/N,AUTO/S

  @{b}Export@{ub}
  FORMAT WIDTH/N,HEIGHT/N,FPS/K,FIT/K,PADCOLOR/K
  EXPORTSETTINGS VIDEO/K,QUALITY/K,SOUND/K,BITRATE/N,RATE/N,TYPE/K
  EXPORT FILE/A,PREVIEW/S
  RENDERSTATUS                   IDLE, RUNNING <pos> <total>, DONE,
                                 FAILED or CANCELLED
  CANCEL

  @{b}Paint programs@{ub}
  GRAB FILE/A,AT/N,FULL/S        save a frame (.png, else IFF ILBM)
  RANGE FROM/N,TO/N,CLEAR/S
  EXPORTRANGE FILE/A,WIDTH/N,FPS/N   poll RENDERSTATUS like EXPORT

@endnode

@node Translations "Translations"

  @{b}Translations@{ub}

  Formbröd follows the language set in the Locale preferences. English
  is built in; Swedish is included.

  To translate it into another language, see locale/ in the source
  code. Translations are very welcome.

@endnode

